cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this software or its experimental results,
  please cite the software using the metadata below.

type: software

title: >
  Robust Pixel-Wise RGB Classification under Poisson Noise:
  TEG-DCT-XGBoost

abstract: >
  Research software for robust pixel-wise classification of RGB remote-sensing
  imagery affected by signal-dependent Poisson noise. The framework combines
  raw RGB values, Texture-Entropy-Gradient (TEG) features, local Discrete Cosine
  Transform (DCT) ring-energy descriptors, Anscombe-based variance stabilization,
  and XGBoost multiclass classification. The implementation supports matched-noise
  robustness evaluation, training-data-efficiency experiments, computational
  profiling, XGBoost feature-importance analysis based on normalized total gain,
  and full-scene classification map generation.

